1962..2036 Comment "/// A path at every loop whose inverse arm drops its rest\'s path: each arm"
2037..2118 Comment "/// checks at its letter, but at `loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q` the loop arm carries"
2119..2190 Comment "/// the inverse arm\'s reflexivity to `Path.here(loop ∷ back(loop) ∷"
2191..2208 Comment "/// q)`, which is"
2209..2284 Comment "/// not the path at `q` the cancellation\'s right side reads. Read as a set,"
2285..2353 Comment "/// the loops would identify the two; the words are not read as one."
